  "claim_boundary": "The high-recovery test used simulated H2/CO/CO2/H2O/H2S gas at about 13.75 bar absolute and 500.8 C, not the final 20-bar H2/CO/CO2/N2/CH4 feed. The 99.9999% pre-leak purity was inferred from an ideal H2/N2 separation factor and is not a component-resolved CO/CO2/N2/CH4 chromatographic measurement. The actual coal-gas test validates model prediction of H2 rate and recovery, but it does not report the final product impurity vector.",
  "interpretation": "The report supplies the missing positive side of the validation hierarchy: sustained high recovery and calculated bulk purity in a multicomponent durability test, plus actual coal-gas model agreement. It supports the feasibility of the project recovery target and physics-model use while leaving component-specific ppm certification open."
